! The spin-spiral twin of h-fcc-magnon.in -- the same crystal, the same grid,
! the same functional -- run through the generalized Bloch theorem instead.
!
! **It exists to confirm the transverse susceptibility by a route that shares no
! machinery with it.** The magnon calculation says the ferromagnet is linearly
! unstable wherever the leading eigenvalue of X_0 F exceeds one, and on this
! cell it says that first at q = (0, 0, 1/4). A scan of E(q) is the independent
! test of the same claim: one is a sum over states plus a matrix inversion on a
! frozen density, the other a sequence of independent self-consistent fields.
!
! **It works, and it did not before, and the difference is one number in this
! file.** Seeded at starting_magnetization = 1.0 -- a fully polarized hydrogen
! atom, with an empty minority channel and a first potential built at
! |zeta| = 1 exactly -- every point of the scan left the magnetic branch, and
! what was recorded was a demagnetization curve rather than a spin-wave energy.
! At 0.9 the branch survives. Measured, conv_thr = 1e-10, 200 iterations
! allowed:
!
!     q_3     converged   iterations      E (Ry)          |m|      E - E(0)
!     0         yes            7       -0.9802841602    0.53125      0.0 meV
!     1/8       yes           10       -0.9849565354    0.40165    -63.6 meV
!     1/4        NO          200       -0.9913133105    0.20020   -150.1 meV
!     3/8       yes           13       -0.9868070126    0.15256    -88.7 meV
!     1/2       yes           59       -0.9846191874    0.04355    -59.0 meV
!
! The minimum is at q = (0, 0, 1/4), which is the wavevector the susceptibility
! named, and it is 150 meV deep. The q = 0 end reproduces the collinear
! ferromagnet of h-fcc-magnon.in to every digit (-0.9802841602 Ry, m = 0.53125),
! which is the check that the spiral machinery reduces correctly at q = 0.
!
! **Three things not to over-read in that table.** The q = 1/4 point does not
! converge -- 1.25e-7 after 200 iterations -- which is what the bottom of a flat
! magnetic surface looks like and is why its energy is quoted to meV and not
! further. The q = 1/8 and 3/8 points are not commensurate with the 4x4x4 grid,
! so their k-sampling is not the same as the other three and the shape of the
! curve between the commensurate points is not converged in the grid. And
! |m| falls monotonically along the scan, so this is a spiral whose moment
! shrinks as it turns, not a rigid rotation of a fixed moment.
!
! **Holding it with `fsm` was tried and this cell cannot be held** (P80). The
! cause is the cell rather than the scheme: m(B) here is nearly a step -- 0.057
! Ry of field takes the moment from 0.027 to 0.719 -- so there is little in
! between to hold, the moment lands saturated, the inner SCF stops converging
! under the field that put it there, and the field then freezes because it only
! steps on converged pairs. Use a robust magnet for a constrained spiral --
! `fe-noncolin-pbe-stress.in` is one.
!
! PLAN.md P63 records the measurement and what replaced it in the tests.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 6.5,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.01,
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.9
    angle1(1) = 90.0
    spiral_q(1) = 0.0, spiral_q(2) = 0.0, spiral_q(3) = 0.0
    nbnd = 8
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 4 0 0 0
